.TH OMORFOS\-SCREENSHOT 1 "" omorfos "omorfos manual"
.nh
.ad l
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
omorfos\-screenshot \- Takes a picture of every screen of the omorfos desktop, and saves it or puts it on the clipboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBomorfos\-screenshot [\-\-window | \-\-pick] [\-\-to WHERE]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Only a program the compositor starts with \fBmay: [capture]\fR may take pictures, and only one with \fBmay: [clipboard]\fR may put them on the clipboard, as the \fBPrint\fR keys start it; run any other way it is refused and says so. \-\-pick needs the \fBpanel\fR and \fBoverlay\fR roles as well, and \-\-window \fBpanel\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR
Take the window with focus, the whole of it, in place of the screens
.TP
\fB\-\-pick\fR
Pick what to take first: drag over an area, or click a window or a screen
.TP
\fB\-\-to file|clipboard|both\fR
Where the picture goes, whatever \fBscreenshots.destination\fR in config.yaml says
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print this help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print the version
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
omorfos\-screenshot
omorfos\-screenshot \-\-pick \-\-to clipboard
omorfos\-screenshot \-\-window \-\-to both
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBomorfos\fR(1), \fBomorfosctl\fR(1), \fBomorfos\-config\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-keys\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-rules\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-menu\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-theme\fR(5)
